  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening and expanding interventions for a consoidation of control for a pre-eradication of Malaria in Senegal - Senegal (01-Jan-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Senegal, Malaria, IntraHealth International, Inc. (IH HQ)This program has the following goals: Decrease malaria related morbidity to reach a level of pre-elimination by 2018.  Decrease malaria related mortality by 75% by 2018. The objectives of this program are: At least 80% of the population sleeps under an LLIN.  Control 100% of epidemics and emergency situations within 2 weeks of detection.  Diagnose at least 95% of suspected malaria cases with rapid diagnostics tests (RDTs) or microscopy.  Protect at least 80% of pregnant women with the intermittent preventive treatment (IPTp) using SP in line with national guidelines.  Treat 100% of confirmed malaria cases according to national guidelines</narrative>
  </description>
